{"dur":555,"ev":[{"t":8.4,"type":"voice","id":"n01","dlg":false,"sub":"At fourteen minutes past six on a Monday evening, Remi Hale would have given anything to have that morning back."},{"t":5.2,"type":"voice","id":"r01","dlg":true,"sub":"Pip! Pip!","who":"Remi"},{"t":18.4,"type":"voice","id":"n02","dlg":false,"sub":"She was about to get it."},{"t":39.6,"type":"voice","id":"n03","dlg":false,"sub":"Twelve hours earlier. Remi had one job that Monday. Be on time."},{"t":45.4,"type":"voice","id":"d01","dlg":true,"sub":"Seven o’clock, Monday morning. Rain by six.","who":"Radio"},{"t":52.6,"type":"voice","id":"r02","dlg":true,"sub":"Seven forty? No. No, no, no!","who":"Remi"},{"t":59,"type":"voice","id":"k01","dlg":true,"sub":"Remi! Will you watch me ride at the park? Six o’clock!","who":"Pip"},{"t":65.2,"type":"voice","id":"r03","dlg":true,"sub":"Can’t, Pip. Big day. Sorry.","who":"Remi"},{"t":77.4,"type":"voice","id":"n04","dlg":false,"sub":"She missed the tram. Then she missed the next one."},{"t":88,"type":"voice","id":"i01","dlg":true,"sub":"You’re forty minutes late, Ms Hale.","who":"Interviewer"},{"t":92.4,"type":"voice","id":"i02","dlg":true,"sub":"Tell me. If you could build anything at all, what would you build?","who":"Interviewer"},{"t":98.3,"type":"voice","id":"r04","dlg":true,"sub":"I… um. I’m sorry. I don’t know.","who":"Remi"},{"t":102.6,"type":"voice","id":"i03","dlg":true,"sub":"We’ll be in touch.","who":"Interviewer"},{"t":106.4,"type":"voice","id":"n05","dlg":false,"sub":"They would not be in touch."},{"t":112.6,"type":"voice","id":"n06","dlg":false,"sub":"On the way home it rained, and Remi ducked into a clock shop she had never noticed before."},{"t":120.6,"type":"voice","id":"w01","dlg":true,"sub":"Ah. A bad day. I have just the thing.","who":"Watchmaker"},{"t":126.6,"type":"voice","id":"w02","dlg":true,"sub":"Turn this knob before you sleep, and you’ll wake up to the same morning. Seven turns. After that, it’s only a clock.","who":"Watchmaker"},{"t":136.8,"type":"voice","id":"r05","dlg":true,"sub":"How much?","who":"Remi"},{"t":139.6,"type":"voice","id":"w03","dlg":true,"sub":"Whatever you think a day is worth.","who":"Watchmaker"},{"t":148.6,"type":"voice","id":"n07","dlg":false,"sub":"One of the first alarm clocks in America was built in 1787. It could only ring at four in the morning, the hour its maker got up for work."},{"t":158.8,"type":"voice","id":"n08","dlg":false,"sub":"Remi’s could do something stranger. She turned the knob."},{"t":167.8,"type":"voice","id":"d02","dlg":true,"sub":"Seven o’clock, Monday morning. Rain by six.","who":"Radio"},{"t":172.8,"type":"voice","id":"r06","dlg":true,"sub":"Monday. Again.","who":"Remi"},{"t":176.4,"type":"voice","id":"n09","dlg":false,"sub":"About two in three people say they have felt déjà vu at least once. Remi was feeling it on purpose."},{"t":183.8,"type":"voice","id":"n10","dlg":false,"sub":"Your body keeps its own clock: about twenty thousand nerve cells, just above the place where your optic nerves cross."},{"t":193.6,"type":"voice","id":"n11","dlg":false,"sub":"Left alone, it runs about eleven minutes longer than a day. Every morning, the light puts it right again."},{"t":205,"type":"voice","id":"k02","dlg":true,"sub":"Remi! Will you watch me ride at the park? Six o’clock!","who":"Pip"},{"t":211,"type":"voice","id":"r07","dlg":true,"sub":"Big day, Pip. Next time.","who":"Remi"},{"t":216.8,"type":"voice","id":"n12","dlg":false,"sub":"So she practised Monday."},{"t":219.6,"type":"voice","id":"r08","dlg":true,"sub":"A bridge. No. A tower?","who":"Remi"},{"t":225,"type":"voice","id":"n13","dlg":false,"sub":"Once you know how something turns out, it feels as if you knew it all along. Psychologists call it hindsight bias."},{"t":233.2,"type":"voice","id":"n14","dlg":false,"sub":"Remi didn’t just feel it. She really did know."},{"t":250.5,"type":"voice","id":"r10","dlg":true,"sub":"A school where every classroom gets the morning sun.","who":"Remi"},{"t":255.4,"type":"voice","id":"i05","dlg":true,"sub":"Ms Hale, that’s the best answer I’ve heard all year. Come back at five. The director wants to meet you.","who":"Interviewer"},{"t":264.8,"type":"voice","id":"r11","dlg":true,"sub":"Yes! I mean, yes. Thank you.","who":"Remi"},{"t":272.8,"type":"voice","id":"n15","dlg":false,"sub":"The final round ran late. Remi didn’t look at the time. It was the perfect Monday."},{"t":280.6,"type":"voice","id":"n16","dlg":false,"sub":"At home, Pip had made her a good luck card. And Pip knew the way to the tram stop."},{"t":301.2,"type":"voice","id":"r12","dlg":true,"sub":"This is my fault. This is all my fault.","who":"Remi"},{"t":305.6,"type":"voice","id":"n17","dlg":false,"sub":"Pip would be all right, the doctors said. In time. But Remi still had turns left."},{"t":314.2,"type":"voice","id":"n18","dlg":false,"sub":"That night, she turned the knob with shaking hands."},{"t":324.6,"type":"voice","id":"r13","dlg":true,"sub":"Pip. Promise me you’ll stay home tonight. Promise.","who":"Remi"},{"t":329.8,"type":"voice","id":"k03","dlg":true,"sub":"Okay, okay! I promise.","who":"Pip"},{"t":335.6,"type":"voice","id":"r14","dlg":true,"sub":"Pick up. Pip, pick up.","who":"Remi"},{"t":339.4,"type":"voice","id":"n19","dlg":false,"sub":"Pip kept her promise. Until she saw the rain, and remembered her sister had no umbrella."},{"t":358,"type":"voice","id":"r15","dlg":true,"sub":"It keeps happening! Whatever I change, it happens at fourteen past six!","who":"Remi"},{"t":364,"type":"voice","id":"w04","dlg":true,"sub":"Because you keep the day you wanted, and only try to change the ending.","who":"Watchmaker"},{"t":370.6,"type":"voice","id":"w05","dlg":true,"sub":"A day isn’t a recording, miss. It’s a promise. You only get to choose who it’s for.","who":"Watchmaker"},{"t":379.6,"type":"voice","id":"n21","dlg":false,"sub":"Every night, your brain replays the day by itself. In rats, scientists watched brain cells repeat the routes of the day while the animals slept."},{"t":389.4,"type":"voice","id":"n22","dlg":false,"sub":"Replaying is the easy part. Choosing is hard."},{"t":393.2,"type":"voice","id":"r16","dlg":true,"sub":"This is the last Monday I can fix.","who":"Remi"},{"t":397,"type":"voice","id":"w06","dlg":true,"sub":"Then don’t fix it. Live it.","who":"Watchmaker"},{"t":403,"type":"voice","id":"k04","dlg":true,"sub":"Remi! Will you watch me ride at the park? Six o’clock!","who":"Pip"},{"t":409.2,"type":"voice","id":"r17","dlg":true,"sub":"Six o’clock. I’ll be there. I promise.","who":"Remi"},{"t":413.4,"type":"voice","id":"k05","dlg":true,"sub":"Really?","who":"Pip"},{"t":417,"type":"voice","id":"i06","dlg":true,"sub":"Come back at five. The director wants to meet you.","who":"Interviewer"},{"t":422,"type":"voice","id":"r18","dlg":true,"sub":"I’m sorry. I can’t. I made a promise.","who":"Remi"},{"t":426.6,"type":"voice","id":"i07","dlg":true,"sub":"Then I’m afraid there won’t be a second chance.","who":"Interviewer"},{"t":431.7,"type":"voice","id":"r19","dlg":true,"sub":"I know.","who":"Remi"},{"t":451,"type":"voice","id":"r20","dlg":true,"sub":"Pip, wait!","who":"Remi"},{"t":455.4,"type":"voice","id":"k06","dlg":true,"sub":"Whoa. That was close.","who":"Pip"},{"t":458.6,"type":"voice","id":"k07","dlg":true,"sub":"You came!","who":"Pip"},{"t":460.8,"type":"voice","id":"r21","dlg":true,"sub":"I’ll always come.","who":"Remi"},{"t":470.6,"type":"voice","id":"n23","dlg":false,"sub":"That night, Remi had one turn left. She didn’t take it."},{"t":492.4,"type":"voice","id":"d03","dlg":true,"sub":"Seven o’clock, Tuesday morning. Sunny all day.","who":"Radio"},{"t":498,"type":"voice","id":"r22","dlg":true,"sub":"Tuesday.","who":"Remi"},{"t":503,"type":"voice","id":"i08","dlg":true,"sub":"Ms Hale, it’s Halden Architects. The director heard why you left. She’d like to meet you on Thursday.","who":"Voicemail"},{"t":522,"type":"voice","id":"n24","dlg":false,"sub":"Remi never turned the knob again. She didn’t need to."},{"t